<title>USA: US DLA sells 210 tonnes surplus tin,avg $5.9238/kg.</title>
<headline>US DLA sells 210 tonnes surplus tin,avg $5.9238/kg.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense Logistics Agency said Wednesday that it accepted two bids for the long-term sale of 210 tonnes of &quot;longhorn&quot; tin for an average $5.9238 per kg.</p>
<p>Awards went to:</p>
<p>-- American Iron &amp; Metal Co, Inc, Montreal, Canada, 200 tonnes at $2.6854 per lb.</p>
<p>-- Zigor 33 Inc, Sunrise, Fla., 10 tonnes at $2.7193 per lb.</p>
<p>The DLA said the next bid opening for longhorn tin will be Dec 4 at 1300 EST.</p>
</text>
